  "faq1Q": "Does it work with the screen off or the app closed?",
  "faq1A": "Yes. Android itself manages the timer with an exact alarm, so it keeps running even if you close the app or turn the screen off.",
  "faq2Q": "Which apps does it work with?",
  "faq2A": "Apps that respond to the Android media controls. It has been tested with the YouTube and Twitch apps; some players may ignore them.",
  "faq3Q": "Why does it ask for the Alarms & reminders permission?",
  "faq3A": "Without it, Android does not allow scheduling an alarm at an exact time and the audio could pause late. It is granted only once from the system settings.",
  "faq4Q": "What is the notification permission for?",
  "faq4A": "To show the countdown with the extend and cancel buttons. If you deny it, the timer still works, just without the notification.",
  "faq5Q": "How do I extend or cancel the timer?",
  "faq5A": "From the notification, with its extend and cancel buttons, without opening the app. You can also cancel from the main screen, or extend with the volume button during the last minute.",
  "faq6Q": "Can I change how much time the extend button adds?",
  "faq6A": "Yes. In Settings, under Extend amount, you can choose between 1 and 60 minutes. The notification button always shows the chosen amount.",
  "faq7Q": "Why does the volume go down during the last minute?",
  "faq7A": "So the audio fades out gradually instead of stopping abruptly. When the time is up, Ziesta pauses the audio and leaves the volume as it was.",
  "faq8Q": "How do I extend the time with the volume button?",
  "faq8A": "While the volume is going down in the last minute, press volume up on your phone: the amount chosen in Settings is added and the volume goes back to what you had. You can turn it off in Settings, under Extend with volume button.",
  "faq9Q": "How do I make the phone lock when the timer ends?",
  "faq9A": "Turn on Lock screen when it ends in Settings. Android will ask you to turn on Ziesta as a device administrator. When the timer ends, Ziesta pauses the audio and locks the phone.",
  "faq10Q": "Why does Ziesta ask to be a device administrator?",
  "faq10A": "Only to be able to lock the screen, and only if you turn that option on. Ziesta uses no other administrator function: it cannot erase data or change your password.",
  "faq11Q": "How do I uninstall Ziesta if I turned on the screen lock?",
  "faq11A": "While Ziesta is an administrator, Android does not allow uninstalling it. Turn off Lock screen when it ends in Settings, or remove its permission in your phone settings (Security, Device administrators), and then uninstall it normally.",
  "faq12Q": "What happens if I restart my phone?",
  "faq12A": "When the phone restarts, Android clears pending alarms, so the timer is cancelled and you would need to set it again.",
  "faq13Q": "Does Ziesta use the internet or collect data?",
  "faq13A": "No. It works offline and does not collect or send any data."
}
